{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One interacts with M19-MEL, through a series of target-mediated pathways involving the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This compound appears to act as a target of multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, all of which are linked to M19-MEL. The shared target of these compounds implies a possible common mechanism of action, likely involving the SDR family member 9, which may be a key mediator in the interaction between the compound and M19-MEL. The evidence suggests that the compound may exert its effects through a direct interaction with SDR family member 9, which in turn influences M19-MEL. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One may modulate M19-MEL through a mechanism involving the SDR family member 9, though further validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
